# Own-wording spells of Valda's Spire of Secrets (2024), chunk 1. TEXT = {name: [summary, full]}.
TEXT = {
"Abduct": ["Teleport a creature within 1 mile to a space near you. Charisma save negates.",
 "Range 1 mile. You must know where the target is. If it is more than 100 ft from the spot you believe it is in while you cast, the spell fails. The target makes a Charisma save. On a fail it teleports to an open space you see within 30 ft of you, and you can have it bound by nearby restraints such as Manacles. When the spell ends, you choose whether it stays where it is or returns to where it came from."],
"Action": ["A willing creature gets an extra action on its next turn: Attack (one weapon attack), Dash, Disengage, Hide or Utilize.",
 "Pick a willing creature you see within 30 ft. During its next turn it gains one extra action. That action can only be Attack (one weapon attack only), Dash, Disengage, Hide or Utilize."],
"Arc Blade": ["Make a melee or ranged spell attack with a weapon, using your casting ability. Deals Lightning or weapon damage.",
 "Lightning runs through the weapon you cast with and you make one attack. It is a melee attack, or a ranged spell attack with range 15 ft as energy leaps off the blade. Use your spellcasting ability for the attack and damage rolls instead of Strength or Dexterity. A ranged hit deals Lightning damage. A melee hit deals Lightning damage or the weapon's normal type, your choice. At levels 5, 11 and 17 the attack adds 1d6, 2d6 and 3d6 Lightning damage."],
"Benign Dismemberment": ["A willing creature can remove body parts painlessly for 1 hour and reattach them. Ritual.",
 "Touch a willing creature. For 1 hour its body parts (fingers, limbs, even the head) can be cut off without harm, as long as the cut is clean and swift. It takes no damage from this. A severed head stays alive and conscious, and parts attached to it do too. Severed parts are inanimate and do not decay while the spell lasts. A held-back part instantly rejoins the stump. When the spell ends, parts still severed stay severed for good. The target dies if its vital organs are not rejoined to its head."],
"Candy Blast": ["Ranged spell attack, 1d8 Force. The target's square becomes Difficult Terrain from a pile of candy for 1 minute.",
 "Hurl a handful of hard candy at a creature you see within 60 ft. Make a ranged spell attack. On a hit the target takes 1d8 Force damage and the candy piles up in its space. A 5-ft square of your choice there becomes Difficult Terrain. The candy is edible but has no nutrition and vanishes after 1 minute, ending the Difficult Terrain. Damage rises by 1d8 at levels 5, 11 and 17."],
"Concealed Shot": ["A Ranged weapon you touch fires silent, invisible shots for 1 minute and need not reveal you.",
 "Touch a Ranged weapon. For 1 minute, when you attack with it, the weapon or ammunition is invisible in flight and the weapon makes no sound. Smoke or light it produces is suppressed. The projectile or weapon becomes visible again after the attack hits or misses. If you are hidden and the target is 80 ft or more away, the attack does not reveal your position."],
"Corruption Curse": ["Curse a creature for up to 1 minute with one of three Disadvantage effects. Concentration.",
 "You glare at a creature you see within 60 ft and send ribbons of dark magic at it. For the duration it is cursed and you choose one effect. Dull Reflexes: Disadvantage on Dexterity checks and saves. Feeble Fortitude: Disadvantage on Constitution saves and it cannot regain HP. Weak Will: Disadvantage on Wisdom saves and spell attack rolls. The save listed for this spell is Constitution."],
"Curse Ward": ["A willing creature gains Necrotic resistance and cannot be cursed or possessed for 8 hours.",
 "Touch a willing creature and raise a smoky barrier around it. For 8 hours it has Resistance to Necrotic damage and cannot be cursed or possessed. If it is already cursed or possessed, that effect is suppressed until the spell ends."],
"Curse of Chains": ["Strength save or a creature is cursed with Speed 0 for up to 1 minute. It can end it with an Athletics check.",
 "A black brand like iron shackles appears on a creature you see within 120 ft. It makes a Strength save or is cursed for the duration. A cursed target has Speed 0 and cannot raise it. It can use an action for a Strength (Athletics) check against your spell save DC, ending the spell on a success."],
"Delay": ["Wisdom save or a creature moves to last place in the Initiative order from the next round on.",
 "You slow time for one creature you see within 60 ft. It makes a Wisdom save. On a fail it is moved to last place in the Initiative order starting at the next round."],
"Eldritch Orb": ["Ranged spell attack, 1d8 Force. The target explodes in a 5-ft Emanation, other creatures take half on a failed Dexterity save.",
 "Fling a ball of eldritch energy at a creature or object within 60 ft. Make a ranged spell attack. On a hit the target takes 1d8 Force damage and explodes in a 5-ft Emanation. Each other creature in the Emanation makes a Dexterity save, taking half the Force damage on a fail and none on a success. Damage rises by 1d8 at levels 5, 11 and 17."],
"Eye of Anubis": ["Two spell attacks, 1d4 Necrotic each, and the target takes a 1d4 penalty on its next attack roll (1d6 if both hit).",
 "Moonlight beams from your eyes. Make two spell attack rolls at one target or two targets within 60 ft. A hit deals 1d4 Necrotic damage and gives the target a 1d4 penalty on the next attack roll it makes before the spell ends at the start of your next turn. If both attacks hit the same target the penalty is 1d6. Each beam's damage rises by 1d4 at levels 5, 11 and 17."],
"Flashback": ["Alter the recent past: you prepared something within the last 24 hours that helps now. The GM sets limits.",
 "Reach back in time and change history slightly, so that you made some preparation in the last 24 hours that helps right now. Describe it to the GM. Examples are having packed a piece of gear or arranged a distraction for this moment. The GM may call for an ability check if it is hard. On a failure the spell fails. Reality changes as little as possible. The spell cannot remove creatures or objects from an encounter, harm a creature, or move creatures or objects you are not wearing or carrying. It can generally add things but not take them away. The GM decides the extent."],
"Force Dart": ["Ranged spell attack, 1d10 Force within 120 ft.",
 "Fling a dart of magical force at a creature within 120 ft. Make a ranged spell attack. On a hit it takes 1d10 Force damage. Damage rises by 1d10 at levels 5, 11 and 17."],
"Frigid Blade": ["Melee spell-strength attack with a weapon coated in ice. Weapon die goes up one step. Deals Cold or weapon damage.",
 "Coat the weapon you cast with in ice and make one melee attack. It uses your spellcasting ability for attack and damage rolls instead of Strength or Dexterity. The weapon's damage die goes up one step (d4, d6, d8, d10, then d12 or 2d6, your choice). It does not change if the weapon has more than one damage die. A hit that deals damage can deal Cold or the weapon's normal type, your choice. At levels 5, 11 and 17 add 1d6, 2d6 and 3d6 Cold damage."],
"Gahoul's Shrieking Skull": ["A skull thrown at a point within 60 ft shrieks. 3d4 Thunder to everyone in a 10-ft Cube, no save. Heard 300 ft.",
 "Throw a cackling skull at a point you see within 60 ft. It emits a shriek that can be heard up to 300 ft away. Each creature in a 10-ft Cube there takes 3d4 Thunder damage, with no save. Using a higher slot: +1d4 for each slot level above 1."],
"Grasp of the Grave": ["Skeletal arms in a 15-ft radius for up to 1 minute: Difficult Terrain, Strength save for 3d6 Force and Prone. Concentration.",
 "Spectral skeletal arms rise from the ground in a 15-ft-radius circle you see within 120 ft. The area is Difficult Terrain for the duration. Each creature you choose in the area makes a Strength save. On a fail it takes 3d6 Force damage and is Prone. Whenever a creature you see enters the area or ends its turn there, you can force that save (once per creature per turn). When a creature tries to leave, you can force a Strength save. On a fail its Speed is 0 until your next turn starts. Using a higher slot: +1d6 for each slot level above 4."],
"Hex: Abate": ["A creature makes a Charisma save or cannot make Opportunity Attacks until the end of your next turn.",
 "One creature you see within 60 ft makes a Charisma save. On a fail it cannot make Opportunity Attacks until the spell ends at the end of your next turn."],
"Hex: Charm": ["Wisdom save or Charmed until the end of your next turn. Ends if you or an ally damage it.",
 "One creature you see within 60 ft makes a Wisdom save, with Advantage if you or an ally are fighting it. On a fail it is Charmed until the spell ends at the end of your next turn. The spell ends early if you or an ally damage it. When it ends, the target knows you charmed it."],
"Hex: Duplicity": ["An illusory double protects you. An attack against you may hit it instead on a d6 roll of 4+.",
 "You create an illusory duplicate of yourself in your space. When a creature hits you with an attack before the spell ends at the end of your next turn, roll a d6. On a 4 or higher the attack hits the duplicate instead and the spell ends. The duplicate ignores all other damage and effects. A creature with Blinded, Blindsight or Truesight is unaffected."],
"Hex: Hallucination": ["Wisdom save or hallucinations until the end of your next turn. You can use a Reaction to give its D20 Tests Disadvantage.",
 "One creature you see within 60 ft makes a Wisdom save or suffers hallucinations until the spell ends at the end of your next turn. Whenever the hallucinating target makes a D20 Test, you can use a Reaction to give that roll Disadvantage."],
"Hex: Misfortune": ["Until the end of your next turn, a natural 20 on the target's D20 Test becomes a 1.",
 "Choose a creature you see within 60 ft. Until the spell ends at the end of your next turn, whenever it rolls a 20 on the d20 of a D20 Test, the roll becomes a 1 instead."],
"Hex: Pox": ["Constitution save or Poisoned until the end of your next turn. Range 10 ft.",
 "One creature you see within 10 ft makes a Constitution save. On a fail it is Poisoned until the spell ends at the end of your next turn."],
"Hex: Tremors": ["5-ft Emanation of shaking ground. Dexterity save or Prone, also for creatures that enter or end their turn there.",
 "The ground shakes in a 5-ft Emanation around you. Each creature on the ground in it makes a Dexterity save or is Prone. A creature that enters the Emanation or ends its turn there must also make the save. The spell ends at the end of your next turn."],
"Hollowing Curse": ["Dexterity save, 2d6 Necrotic and cursed. Later turns you deal more damage with an action or half with a Bonus Action. Concentration.",
 "Tendrils of draining mist reach out from your fingers. A creature you see within 60 ft makes a Dexterity save. On a fail it takes 2d6 Necrotic damage and is cursed for the duration. On a success it takes half damage only. On each later turn you can use a Magic action or Bonus Action to damage the cursed creature: 2d6 Necrotic for the Magic action, half that for the Bonus Action. Using a higher slot: +2d6 for each slot level above 1."],
"Impressions of the Past": ["See your location as it was up to 100 years ago, for up to 1 minute. You cannot move or speak. Concentration.",
 "Cast your senses back in time to perceive where you stand as it was at a moment you name, up to 100 years ago, including events then. The past looks dreamlike and shadowy. You can look in any direction, see detail and hear speech, but you cannot move or speak."],
"Intensify Gravity": ["50-ft-radius, 100-ft-high Cylinder of heavy gravity: double movement cost, double weight, no flying, double fall damage. Concentration.",
 "Gravity grows stronger in a Cylinder (50-ft radius, 100 ft high) centered on a point within 100 ft. A creature there spends 2 ft of movement per 1 ft moved (3 ft with Difficult Terrain). A Prone creature that tries to stand must succeed on a Strength check against your spell save DC or its Speed is 0 until the end of the turn. Objects there, including worn and carried ones, weigh double, which may encumber creatures or break spells with a weight limit such as Levitate. Fly Speeds in the area drop to 0. Creatures and objects take double damage from falling."],
"Jethro's Instant Reload": ["A Ranged weapon reloads itself for 8 hours and ignores the DM-C, LD and RLD properties.",
 "Enchant one Ranged weapon you touch to reload itself. For 8 hours, if it has the DM-C, LD or RLD property, you ignore that property. When its ammunition runs out, ammunition you carry teleports into it."],
"Magic Daggers": ["Two force daggers thrown at targets within 30 ft, each a ranged spell attack for 1d6 Force. More daggers at higher levels.",
 "Conjure two daggers of magical force and flick them at targets within 30 ft, at one target or several. Make a separate ranged spell attack for each dagger. A hit deals 1d6 Force damage. The daggers vanish after the attack. You create one more dagger and make one more attack at levels 5 (3), 11 (4) and 17 (5)."],
"Map": ["Create a gridded map (50-ft square, 5-ft grid) of the area within 60 ft. Shows fixed objects only. Ritual.",
 "Magically draw a gridded map of an area you choose within 60 ft. It shows a 50-ft square on a 5-ft grid with scale-accurate details of non-moving objects, without color. It omits secret doors, traps and creatures. In a multi-level structure it shows only the level you cast it on."],
"Minor Lifesteal": ["Constitution save or 1d6 Necrotic, and you gain Temporary HP equal to the damage.",
 "Try to drain life from a creature you see within 60 ft. It makes a Constitution save or takes 1d6 Necrotic damage. You gain Temporary HP equal to the damage dealt. Damage rises by 1d6 at levels 5, 11 and 17."],
"Perforating Shot": ["Bonus Action on an attack: the weapon becomes a 5-ft Line of energy. Dexterity save for Force damage equal to the weapon's.",
 "As your attack hits or misses its target, the weapon or ammunition becomes a 5-ft-wide Line of magical energy that runs out to the weapon's normal range and includes the original target. Each creature in the Line makes a Dexterity save, taking Force damage equal to the weapon's normal damage on a fail and half on a success. Using a higher slot: the weapon's damage rises by 1d8 for each slot level above 1."],
"Pharaoh's Curse": ["Constitution save or cursed with mummy rot: no healing, HP maximum falls 3d6 every 24 hours. Lasts until dispelled.",
 "Release a puff of dust carrying mummy rot at one creature within 10 ft. It makes a Constitution save or is cursed until dispelled. While cursed it cannot regain HP, its HP maximum does not return to normal after a Long Rest, and its HP maximum drops by 3d6 for every 24 hours that pass. A creature reduced to 0 HP by the curse dies and turns to dust."],
"Protect Threshold": ["Ward a doorway or window for 10 minutes. An unseen creature deals 4d6 Psychic (Wisdom save for half) to those who pass. Ritual.",
 "Trace sigils along the edge of a doorway, window or other portal you touch. For 10 minutes an Invisible eldritch creature guards it. A creature that tries to pass makes a Wisdom save, taking 4d6 Psychic damage on a fail or half on a success. Using a higher slot: +1d6 for each slot level above 2."],
"Proto-Enchantment": ["Wisdom save to Charm, Frighten, and at higher slots Frenzy (3+) or Stun (5+) a creature within 30 ft. Concentration.",
 "Manipulate the mind of a creature you see within 30 ft with one option. The target makes a Wisdom save for each. Charm: Charmed for the duration, with Advantage on the save if you or your companions are fighting it. It ends if you or a companion harm it. Frighten: Frightened for the duration, repeating the save at each turn end. Frenzy (slot 3+): Frenzied for the duration. It sees everyone as an enemy, picks attack targets at random from creatures it sees in range, and must make Opportunity Attacks. It repeats the save at each turn end. Stun (slot 5+): Stunned for the duration, repeating the save at each turn end. This is a Protospell."],
"Proto-Transmutation": ["Ritual-length transmutation: change a gallon of water, or an object's material, or at slot 5+ a willing Humanoid's species.",
 "Choose one option. Transmute Liquid: touch a vessel holding 1 gallon of water and turn it into a vial of Acid, a flask of Alchemist's Fire, a vial of Basic Poison, 1 pint of honey, a flask of Oil, 1 quart of vinegar or a bottle of Common Wine. Transmute Solid: touch an object that is not worn or carried and change parts within a 1-ft Cube made wholly of crystal, glass, ice, iron, steel, stone or wood into another of those materials. The part's AC changes to match. Transmute Humanoid (slot 5+): touch a willing Humanoid to change its look and species. It picks a new species, loses its old species' traits and gains the new ones, and decides its appearance. This is a Protospell."],
"Restore Youth": ["An 8-hour ritual makes a creature look 2d10 years younger (not under 18). Does not extend lifespan.",
 "Perform a long ritual on a creature you touch to reduce its apparent age by 2d10 years, to a minimum of 18. It does not lengthen the creature's life."],
"Rumor": ["Spread a rumor of up to 10 words in a 100-ft Emanation for 1 minute. Listeners think nearby people are repeating it.",
 "Spread a rumor of 10 words or fewer in a 100-ft Emanation around you. A creature there that can hear and understand three or more other creatures believes it hears the rumor repeated by someone nearby. Each creature hears it from a different person, so its origin cannot be traced. A rumor will not usually make creatures Hostile, but it can shift their attitude for better or worse."],
"Scurry": ["An object up to 10 lb sprouts legs and runs 20 ft per turn in a direction you choose. AC 10.",
 "Choose a nonmagical object within 60 ft that weighs 10 lb or less and is not worn. It may be carried if it is not wrapped fully around a body or held in a hand: a drawstring pouch on a belt works, a helmet or a held sword does not. The object wriggles free, grows two legs and moves 20 ft in a direction you choose, which you can change at the start of each of your turns. It has AC 10 unless higher. The spell ends early if it drops to 0 HP or is picked up."],
"Solar Wind": ["Dexterity save or 1d8 Radiant and pushed 10 ft.",
 "A gust of solar radiance hits a creature you see within 60 ft. It makes a Dexterity save or takes 1d8 Radiant damage and is pushed 10 ft away from you. Damage rises by 1d8 at levels 5, 11 and 17."],
"Springheel": ["Bonus Action: Long and High Jumps go 10 ft farther and need no run-up until your next turn starts.",
 "Pour magic into your legs. Until the start of your next turn, your Long Jump and High Jump distance rises by 10 ft (the extra distance costs movement as usual) and you take no penalty for a standing jump."],
"Suspend": ["Bonus Action: pause a condition, spell, ability score reduction or HP maximum reduction on a creature for 1 hour.",
 "Temporarily end one effect on a creature you see within 60 ft. It resumes when the spell ends. Choose one: a condition (Blinded, Deafened, Paralyzed, Petrified or Poisoned), a spell on the target (its duration pauses and the caster need not keep Concentration until this spell ends), a reduction to one ability score, or a reduction to its HP maximum."],
"Thunderous Echo": ["10-ft Cone of noise: Constitution save or 1d6 Thunder. Casting it again by your next turn's end amplifies it to 1d8.",
 "Produce a wave of sound in a 10-ft Cone that can be heard 100 ft away. Each creature in the area makes a Constitution save or takes 1d6 Thunder damage. An echo lingers for the duration. If you cast the spell again before the end of your next turn, it is amplified and deals 1d8 instead. Damage rises by 1d6 (or 1d8 if amplified) at levels 5, 11 and 17."],
"Watery Tentacles": ["Four water tentacles for up to 1 minute: Strength save, 2d8 Bludgeoning and Restrained. Concentration.",
 "Four water tentacles appear around you. Direct each at a creature you see within 30 ft to force a Strength save (once per creature per turn). On a fail it takes 2d8 Bludgeoning damage and is Restrained until the spell ends. A Restrained creature repeats the Strength save at each of its turn ends and takes the damage again on a fail. A tentacle is destroyed when a creature saves against it. As a Magic action you can move each Restrained creature up to 30 ft, direct tentacles to try to Restrain a creature within 30 ft of you, or move a Huge or smaller object that is not worn or carried. Using a higher slot: one more tentacle per slot level above 4."],
"Word of Force": ["Bonus Action: Strength save or 1d6 Force, pushed 10 ft and Prone. Half damage on a save.",
 "Speak a word of force to a creature you see within 30 ft. It makes a Strength save. On a fail it takes 1d6 Force damage, is pushed 10 ft away and is Prone. On a success it takes half damage only. Using a higher slot: +1d6 for each slot level above 1."],
"Zero Gravity": ["30-ft-radius Sphere with no gravity for up to 1 minute: creatures drift and can only push off fixed surfaces. Concentration.",
 "Create zero gravity in a 30-ft-radius Sphere centered on a point you see within 100 ft. Creatures and objects hang in the air until moved. A creature can only move by pushing or pulling on a fixed object or surface within reach, moving as if climbing. Otherwise its Speed is 0. Once set in motion, a creature or object keeps moving at the same Speed each turn until it hits an obstacle. Things in the area are weightless but may still be hard to move. When the spell ends, anything in the air falls unless held up."],
}
